Within the framework of the three-body QCD sum rule pouch model, we have conducted an in-depth analysis of the semileptonic decays of doubly charmed baryons, focusing on the transitions $\Xi_{cc}^{\pm} 	o \Lambda_c^{+} \mu^{-} ar{
u}_{\mu}$, $\Xi_{cc}^{+} 	o \Lambda_c^{+} \pi^{+}\mu^{-} ar{
u}_{\mu}$, and $\Xi_{cc}^{+} 	o \Omega_c^{0} \pi^{+}\mu^{-} ar{
u}_{\mu}$. Our findings reveal that the partial decay widths for these transitions are on the order of $10^{-14}$ to $10^{-15}$ GeV, indicating that these decays are extremely rare.
